---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { network, forms } from '../lib/network';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
import { publishedLabs, institutionsOf } from '../lib/labs';

const labs = await publishedLabs();
const institutions = institutionsOf(labs.filter((l) => l.data.tier === 'member'));
const docs = (await getCollection('docs', (d) => !d.data.draft && d.data.audience === 'public')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order || a.data.title.localeCompare(b.data.title, 'en'),
);
---

<Base title="About" description={network.mission}>
  <h1>About the network</h1>
  {network.name_native && <p class="muted">{network.name_native}</p>}
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lead">{network.mission}</p>
    <p>
      It is a network, not a registered society. There is no membership fee, no legal entity and no president. What
      exists is an agreement among labs to host seminars together, keep a public roster, share teaching material and
      let any member invite a speaker on behalf of all. If the network ever needs a legal form, that decision will be
      taken openly and recorded in the charter.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Computational and cognitive neuroscience in the Greater Bay Area is spread across many campuses, each with a
      handful of labs. No single department has the audience to justify inviting the speakers its members want to
      hear, and no existing society spans the border between Hong Kong, Macau and Guangdong. Pooling the audience and
      the invitations solves both problems at once. The site is the network's public face; the day-to-day
      conversation happens in a group chat and on the announcement list.
    </p>

    <h2>Working language</h2>
    <p>
      The site and the seminars are in English, the one language that belongs to nobody in a region whose labs work in
      Cantonese, Mandarin and English. Names may be listed in native script beside the Latin form. Teaching material
      may be in any language and is labelled.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is run</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Coordinators.</strong> A small group, one per participating institution where possible, keeps the
        seminar calendar, reviews submissions and holds the keys to this repository. Coordinators rotate; the current
        list is below.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rotating hosts.</strong> Each seminar is hosted by one member lab in turn. The host invites the speaker,
        chairs the session and circulates the link.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Two tiers.</strong> Member labs are based in the Greater Bay Area. Affiliate labs elsewhere take part
        and are listed with a badge. Both are reviewed before listing.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Delisting.</strong> A lab is removed when its PI asks or leaves the region, and the roster is refreshed
        annually.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Everything in the open.</strong> The roster, the calendar, the charter and this site are files in a
        public repository. Changes are pull requests anyone can read.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Coordinators</h2>
  {network.coordinators.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="muted">To be announced.</p>
  ) : (
    <ul class="speaker-list">
      {network.coordinators.map((c) => (
        <li>
          <strong>{c.url ? <a href={c.url}>{c.name}</a> : c.name}</strong>
          {c.name_native && <span class="muted"> {c.name_native}</span>}
          <span class="muted"> · {c.institution} · {c.role}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  )}

  {institutions.length > 0 && (
    <>
      <h2>Participating institutions</h2>
      <ul class="chips">
        {institutions.map((i) => (
          <li class="chip accent" title={i.city}>{i.name}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </>
  )}
  {network.host_institutions.length > 0 && (
    <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:0.75rem">
      Hosting institutions for the seminar series: {network.host_institutions.join(', ')}.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2>Documents</h2>
  {docs.length === 0 ? (
    <p class="muted">The charter and other documents are being drafted.</p>
  ) : (
    <ul>
      {docs.map((d) => (
        <li>
          <a href={url(`docs/${d.id}/`)}>{d.data.title}</a>
          {d.data.summary && <span class="muted"> · {d.data.summary}</span>}
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  )}
  <p class="small"><a href={url('docs/')}>All documents, including coordinator handbooks</a></p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {network.contact_email ? (
      <>Email <a href={`mailto:${network.contact_email}`}>{network.contact_email}</a>, or </>
    ) : (
      <>The contact address is being set up. Meanwhile, </>
    )}
    open an issue in the <a href={forms.issues}>repository</a>. Seminar announcements go out on the calendar
    feed and the announcement list.
  </p>
</Base>
